<title>SINGAPORE: CAM Int full yr net profits down sharply.</title>
<headline>CAM Int full yr net profits down sharply.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     3.36  vs 8.36</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.5   vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    1.4   vs 3.5</p>
<p>    Turnover			     127.16  vs 130.56</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	1.41  vs 0.45</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   3.08  vs 1.44</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     7.08  vs 7.16</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 4.08  vs 8.40</p>
<p>    Tax					0.72  vs 0.04</p>
<p>Dividend pay date:  April 23, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: March 31, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Precision engineering group Cam International said performance was affected by the slowdown in the electronics industry. It expects satisfactory results for the half year to end March 1997.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
